\begin_layout Section
Install Eclipse, R, ImageJ Plugins or Packages in Bio7
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Install-Eclipse,-R,"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 can be extended with Eclipse plugins, R packages, Python packages, Java libraries, ImageJ plugins and custom scripts (scripts which extend a menu or are executed at startup):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Eclipse plugins are installed with the update manager (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "chap:Update-Manager"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
R packages are installed with the Packages view of the R perspective or with the R command line.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Python packages are installed with the Python Packages view (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:The-Python-Perspective"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Java libraries are added in the preferences of the dynamic compiler, also downloaded from Maven (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Java-Libraries"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
ImageJ plugins (*.class or *.jar files) are installed in the plugins folder of ImageJ (Bio7/plugins/com.eco.bio7.image_x.x.x/plugins) or dropped on the ImageJ-Canvas view (
\series bold
Plugins > Install...
\series default
 of ImageJ).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Scripts (Java, R, Python, Groovy, BeanShell, JavaScript and ImageJ macros) can be placed in special folders to extend the menus of Bio7 or to be executed at startup. The folders are set in 
\series bold
Preferences Bio7
\series default
 (
\series bold
Script location
\series default
). Subfolders become submenus, an underscore in a file name is displayed as a space.
\end_layout

