\begin_layout Standard
The browser is used for the R help, for R Markdown and Quarto documents (*.html, *.pdf) and for interactive charts of Python. In the browser preferences (
\series bold
Preferences Bio7 > Preferences R > Preferences Browser
\series default
) PDF files can be embedded in the Browser view (
\series bold
Embed PDF in browser view
\series default
), the URL of the help for the installation of R packages can be changed and JavaScript scripts of the JavaScript editor can be executed in the current browser page (
\series bold
Execute JavaScript editor script in current browser
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Uninstall Eclipse Plugins
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Help > About Bio7 > Installation Details
\series default
 lists the installed plugins: plugins can be uninstalled there, and the 
\series bold
Installation History
\series default
 reverts the installation of Bio7 to an earlier state. In this way a corrupted installation can be reverted to a previous state.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Programming Examples for Bio7
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Programming-Examples"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The examples of Bio7 are available on GitHub: 
\begin_inset Flex URL
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
https://github.com/Bio7/bio7_examples
\end_layout

\end_inset

. The repository contains a project for each language:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Bio7_Java_Examples:
\series default
 Java examples for the components of Bio7, e.g., the simulation API, models (2D and 3D), OpenGL, ImageJ, R and Python from Java, GUIs (also WindowBuilder GUIs with their Shiny and JavaScript apps), GDAL, WorldWind, flows, deep learning and profiling.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Bio7_R_Examples, Bio7_Python_Examples:
\series default
 the R and Python APIs of Bio7, simulations, OpenCV and snippets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Bio7_Groovy_Examples, Bio7_BeanShell_Examples, Bio7_JavaScript_Examples, Bio7_ImageJ_Macro_Examples:
\series default
 examples for the other script languages, e.g., ImageJ, R, the Bio7 GUI, LibreOffice and image clustering.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Bio7_Flow_Examples, Bio7_Data:
\series default
 flows with their components and the data of the 3D measurements.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Download the repository as a ZIP file and import the projects with 
\series bold
File > Import > Existing Projects into Workspace
\series default
 (
\series bold
Select archive file
\series default
). The paths of the Java examples are adapted after a confirmation (in a Git clone they have to be adjusted by hand).
\end_layout


